kedby":[]},{"date":"2021-02-10T16:43:15-08:00","id":1435121,"title":"","content":"Without giving too much away there is time travel involved. Therefore someone or some people are in the same time at different places. As a result in this instance someone is breaking 3 of these rules, from a certain perspective. <br /> <br /> I would like to throw red herrings too.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/19533-pnizzle","name":"Pnizzle","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar19533_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"383"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-02-11T04:56:14-08:00","id":1435173,"title":"","content":"Well time travel breaks one or two of the classics:<br /> <br /> There are no do overs<br /> No take backs<br /> <br /> There's also some basic rules about solid things being solid, light casting shadows, etc. <br /> <br /> You might also consider throwing some folk wisdom rules in, such as:<br /> <br /> Home is where the heart is<br /> <br /> <br /> Of course, how inviolable these rules are is up to you. I think Mage generally takes the approach of the hidden rule: If you do any of these things, don't get caught.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Mage: The Ice-ension: An Epic Game of Reality on the Rink","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/758-ramnesis","name":"Ramnesis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar758_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2220"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}